---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "gallery", label: "Shapes" },
  { id: "media", label: "Images and videos" },
  { id: "buttons", label: "Buttons" },
  { id: "notes", label: "Notes" },
]);
const shapes = [
  "pebble", "bean", "peak", "dart", "slice",
  "kite", "cell", "crest", "facet", "spark",
  "seal", "scallop-4", "scallop-6", "scallop-7", "scallop-9",
  "scallop-12", "bloom-4", "bloom-8", "spike", "flare",
];
---
<DocsLayout page="shapes">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.gallery}>
    <p>Add a <code>.shape-*</code> class to cut an element to one of twenty rounded shapes.
      The set follows the Material 3 Expressive shape library. The shape is a mask, so it
      scales with the element and its curves stay smooth at any size. No JavaScript is needed.</p>
    <div class="shape-gallery">
      {shapes.map(name => (
        <figure>
          <div class={`shape-${name}`}></div>
          <figcaption><code>{name}</code></figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.media}>
    <p>On an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code>,
      the class also sets <code>aspect-ratio: 1</code> and <code>object-fit: cover</code>,
      so the picture is cropped to a square instead of stretching the shape. Set the width;
      the height follows.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 align-center">
      <img class="shape-scallop-9" width="160" src="https://picsum.photos/id/1025/400/300" alt="A pug wrapped in a blanket">
      <img class="shape-bloom-4" width="160" src="https://picsum.photos/id/1015/400/400" alt="A river between mountains">
      <img class="shape-pebble" width="160" src="https://picsum.photos/id/64/400/400" alt="A portrait of a woman">
    </div>
    <Code code={`<img class="shape-scallop-9" width="160" src="pug.jpg" alt="A pug wrapped in a blanket">
<video class="shape-bloom-4" width="240" src="clip.mp4" controls></video>`} />
    <p>Native video controls sit at the edges of the box, where most shapes cut them off.
      Use custom controls, or keep <code>controls</code> off for decorative loops.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.buttons}>
    <p>The shapes are drawn for a square box, so pair them with icon buttons, FABs, or
      a button with equal width and height. A wide button stretches the shape.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 align-center">
      <button class="icon-button filled large shape-spark" type="button" aria-label="Favorite">
        <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">favorite</span>
      </button>
      <button class="icon-button tonal large shape-scallop-6" type="button" aria-label="Edit">
        <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">edit</span>
      </button>
      <button class="icon-button filled large shape-bloom-4" type="button" aria-label="Add">
        <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
      </button>
      <button class="btn shape-flare" type="button" style="width: 96px; height: 96px">New</button>
    </div>
    <Code code={`<button class="icon-button filled large shape-spark" type="button" aria-label="Favorite">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">favorite</span>
</button>
<button class="btn shape-flare" type="button" style="width: 96px; height: 96px">New</button>`} />
    <p>The mask would clip the usual focus outline, so a focused shape draws its ring inside
      its own edge: a 3px band in the secondary color and a 2px gap. Press
      <kbd>Tab</kbd> to see it. Forced-colors mode paints the band in <code>Highlight</code>.
      Clicks and taps on the cut-away parts of the box pass through to the page behind.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.notes}>
    <p>The class adds <code>contain: paint</code>, which clips overflowing content and makes
      the element the containing block for absolutely positioned children. Shadows and
      borders are cut with the rest of the element. Wrap the element if it needs a shadow
      that follows the shape, and apply <code>filter: drop-shadow()</code> to the wrapper.</p>
    <p>For a selective Sass build, include <code>"shapes"</code> in <code>$utilities</code>.</p>
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .shape-gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(5.5rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .shape-gallery figure { margin: 0; text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; }
  .shape-gallery div {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    margin: 0 auto 0.5rem;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
  }
</style>
